[32;1m[1;3mQuestion: A boat dealership needs to allocate different types of boats into different display areas. Specifically, the dealership has several display areas, each with a capacity limit provided in “capacity.csv.” The predefined value and size of each boat type can be found in “products.csv.” The objective is to determine the optimal number of units of each boat type to place in each display area to maximize the total value of the boats across all areas, while ensuring that the total size of the boats in each area does not exceed its capacity. The decision variables x_{ij} represent the number of units of boat type j to be placed in display area i.The decision variables must be integers.

Thought: I need to formulate an abstract integer programming model for this allocation problem. I will define index sets for display areas and boat types, parameters for capacities, values, and sizes, integer variables for allocation, and write the objective and constraints symbolically. I will also provide a Data Mapping that identifies the exact table and column names for each parameter.

Final Answer:

#### Index Sets

- $I$: set of display areas (from capacity.csv)
- $J$: set of boat types (from products.csv)

#### Parameters

- $C_i$: capacity of display area $i$ (from capacity.csv, column "capacity")
- $v_j$: value of one unit of boat type $j$ (from products.csv, column "value")
- $s_j$: size of one unit of boat type $j$ (from products.csv, column "size")

#### Decision Variables

- $x_{ij} \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$: number of units of boat type $j$ placed in display area $i$

#### Objective

$$
\max \sum_{i \in I} \sum_{j \in J} v_j \cdot x_{ij}
$$

#### Constraints

1. **Capacity constraints for each display area:**
   $$
   \sum_{j \in J} s_j \cdot x_{ij} \leq C_i, \quad \forall i \in I
   $$

2. **Non-negativity and integrality:**
   $$
   x_{ij} \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}, \quad \forall i \in I, \forall j \in J
   $$

---

#### Data Mapping

- $I$: All rows in capacity.csv, column "display_area_id"
- $C_i$: capacity.csv, column "capacity"
- $J$: All rows in products.csv, column "product_id"
- $v_j$: products.csv, column "value"
- $s_j$: products.csv, column "size"[0m

